-- ============================================================
-- LiAInne — Consolidated Schema
-- ============================================================
-- This replaces the pasted-together migration history in
-- sql_queries. What changed:
--
--   • Removed duplicate / conflicting table definitions:
--       goals, goal_tasks, journal_entries, skill_progress,
--       daily_plans, and habits were each defined twice with
--       different columns. Folded down to one definition per
--       table, matching what main.py actually reads/writes.
--   • Folded standalone ALTER TABLE patches (board_quest_tasks
--       habit-link columns, journal_entries entry_type/energy/
--       focus, journal_entries.tags) into the base CREATE TABLE
--       so a fresh DB doesn't need them run separately.
--   • Dropped dead columns nothing in main.py ever reads or
--       writes: journal_entries.goal_progress, goals.tags.
--   • Fixed a real bug: habit_synergies.synergy_key and
--       .habits_involved were NOT NULL with no default, but
--       _check_and_apply_synergies() in main.py only ever
--       inserts name/bonus_desc/expires_at/created_at — every
--       synergy insert was failing against that constraint.
--       See the ALTER block near the bottom.
--   • Simplified match_entries() to the columns
--       build_semantic_matches_block() actually uses (it never
--       reads goal_progress from the match rows).
--   • Ordered tables by FK dependency so this runs top-to-bottom
--       on a fresh database with no forward references.
--
-- Safe to run on an existing database: every CREATE TABLE uses
-- IF NOT EXISTS, so already-existing tables are left untouched.
-- The one exception is the habit_synergies NOT NULL fix, which
-- is an explicit, idempotent ALTER — see that section.
-- ============================================================


